<title>USA: IES merger wins preliminary nod in Illinois.</title>
<headline>IES merger wins preliminary nod in Illinois.</headline>
<dateline>CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>An administrative law judge on Monday recommended that the Illinois Commerce Commission approve a proposed merger involving IES Industries Inc, WPL Holdings Inc and Interstate Power Co, IES said.</p>
<p>The partners have proposed the formation of Interstate Energy Corp, which requires the approval of four state utility commissions and four federal regulatory agencies, IES said. The deal was announced in November 1995.</p>
<p>The Illinois Commerce Commission is expected to make a final ruling in the next few months. All remaining approvals are expected by the end of the third quarter, IES said.</p>
<p>IES is a public utility company.</p>
<p>Its shares closed unchanged Monday at 29-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
